===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A thing that [[hold]]s.
#: {{ux|en|Put your umbrella in the umbrella '''holder'''.}}
# A person who temporarily or permanently possesses something.
#: {{ux|en|He's been an account '''holder''' with us since 2004.}}
#: {{ux|en|In 2012, there were 28 living '''holders''' of the [[Victoria Cross]] or the [[George Cross]].}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1881|author=w:George Saintsbury|chapter=Dryden|title=English Men of Letters
|passage=Davenant, the last '''holder''' of the laureateship, had died two years previously, and Howell, the well known author of the ''Epistolæ Ho-Elianæ'', and the late '''holder''' of the historiographership, four years before.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=Villainage in England|journal=The English Historical Review|volume=VII|issue=XXVII|location=London|publisher=[[w:Longman|Longmans, Green, and Co.]]; New York, N.Y.:{{nb...|15 East 16th Street}}|month=July|year=1892|page=460|passage=How many of these gafolgelders by contract were to be found on Saxon manors, whether on the lord’s demesne or holding virgates in the open fields, ''libere tenentes'' or free '''holders''' of villain holdings, as I have elsewhere stated we cannot tell, but if we may take the experience of the interval between the Domesday survey and the hundred rolls as any guide to the natural multiplication of ''libere tenentes'' on the lord’s demesne, the class may have become numerous on many, and perhaps mostly on royal manors, without giving ground, I think, for any inference in favour of the original freedom of the Saxon village community.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1996|author=United States. Internal Revenue Service|title=Internal Revenue Bulletin|isbn=|page=47|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=OHSYuePiy4kC&
|passage=A request for a nonreviewable ruling must be submitted by an issuer or '''holder'''.}}
# {{lb|en|nautical}} One who is employed in the hold of a vessel.
# {{lb|en|sports}} The defending champion.

